[youtube]2eowYOEa5dw[/youtube][/center]

[size=4][b]🆕 What's New in v1.6[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]New:[/b] DDS mip inspection — [b]Ctrl + [[/b] / [b]Ctrl + ][/b] step mip levels; right-click [b]Mip Level[/b] picks a level. Current mip and source dimensions show in the info bar[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Channel isolation — [b]R[/b] / [b]G[/b] / [b]B[/b] / [b]A[/b] show one channel as grayscale; [b]N[/b] restores RGBA (D3D path)[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Alpha Channel override — right-click chooses Auto / Transparency / Opaque (data). Encoding (straight/premultiplied) is kept separate from usage so data-bearing alpha no longer darkens colors by mistake[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Image Information — press [b]I[/b] (or use the context menu) for path, format, mip, alpha, channel, and view state[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Compare up to [b]8[/b] viewers in an equal-width grid (5–6 panes: 2×3; 7–8 panes: 2×4)[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Open Recent (MRU) from the right-click menu, with Clear Recent Files[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Save Pane Screenshot from the composed offscreen frame — not blocked by overlapping windows[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] BSA archive browsing alongside ZIP / 7Z / RAR / BA2; archive readers are cached for snappier large-pack browsing[/*]
[*][b]New:[/b] Thumbnail-strip horizontal scrollbar when the strip overflows[/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] Path / info bar tooltips; right-click the path to copy it[/*]
[*][b]Changed:[/b] Hotkeys — navigation toggle is now [b]Alt + N[/b], sampling quality is [b]Alt + Q[/b], alpha checkerboard is [b]Alt + A[/b] ([b]N[/b] is used to restore RGBA after channel isolation)[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]What's New in v1.5[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]New:[/b] Image rotation — rotate the current image 90° with the [b]<[/b] / [b]>[/b] keys, or use the right-click menu for Rotate Left/Right, Rotate 180°, and Reset Rotation. The current angle is shown next to the zoom percentage[/*]
[*][b]Fixed:[/b] Rotated images no longer lose their aspect ratio — they now stay correctly proportioned at any rotation[/*]
[*][b]Fixed:[/b] Panning a rotated image now follows the mouse in the correct direction[/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] Eliminated a brief freeze (roughly 1–5 seconds) that could occur shortly after opening a large folder, caused by many thumbnail loading spinners finishing at the same moment[/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] Slightly smaller executable size from further internal cleanup[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]What's New in v1.41[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Fixed:[/b] When opening two files with the same filename from different folders in quick succession, both could open as separate windows instead of a side-by-side comparison — now reliably opens as a split pane[/*]
[*][b]Improved:[/b] Startup is noticeably faster — the window now restores its last position instantly, without an extra OS round-trip that previously added ~50 ms[/*]
[/list]

